> Good to know: Paid a flat monthly payment for a car? Its statement shows a Flat monthly payment line for the month (a part month by the day) instead of the Revenue Share. The car''s rentals are listed without amounts paid to you, as CarmaCars keeps them, and there is no insurance or tracker fee for it. A booking expense is taken off only when we charge it to you; it then shows as an owner cost with its reason. Vehicles shows the amount and since when.

### Fees taken from your statement
If you agreed with CarmaCars to have your fees taken from your revenue statement, your invoices are not debited from your bank account. Each invoice is paid from your next owner statement (the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement") and reads **Paid from statement**. If a statement does not cover it, the rest is taken from the next one; an invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date is debited from your bank account after the usual notice.

### A flat monthly payment and your agreement
If your cars are paid a flat monthly amount, your Enrollment Agreement is the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement**: a fixed Monthly Amount per car on the payout date, part months by the day, no revenue share and no insurance or tracker fee. When your pay changes from one way to the other, Home shows **Check and sign** for the new agreement.

## Repairs and partner credits

If CarmaCars turns it on for you, **Money** > **Statements** also shows the repair costs and partner credits on your own cars this year, with who paid each repair. It is not part of your statements or payouts.

## Statement periods and price limits (release 35)

- Each statement covers the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th pays it. A rental across the cutoff is paid for the days in each period, never twice.
- Amounts a renter still owes are listed apart on your statement and paid on the statement after we collect them.
- Set the lowest and highest daily rate for every car or one car: short-notice pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers stay between them.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your fees are debited from your bank account on the 15th, after a notice. Your payout for the month before arrives on the 10th, with a statement.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-how-your-fees-work" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How your fees work</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Each car has two monthly fees: an insurance fee and a tracker fee. They are due every month, rented or not.</li><li>The tracker fee starts the day the car&#39;s tracker is installed. The tracker install fee has its own invoice.</li><li>Before a car goes live you pay the first and last month amount we agreed with you (usually two months of the insurance fee, or the exact amount we agreed).</li><li>Your amounts are the ones we agreed for each car, to the cent. Any other fee we agreed, for example a registration fee, comes on its own invoice with each line, its quantity and whether HST applies.</li><li>Cars shows each car&#39;s terms: the insurance fee and tracker fee a month and the Revenue Share, since when they apply, and any change coming. Open a car for its History: every period of terms and every notice we sent (Download the notice).</li><li>Lower amounts apply from the date in our notice. A higher fee comes with 30 days&#39; written notice; a higher Revenue Share applies only if you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. A month whose fee changes part way is billed per day at each amount.</li><li>One invoice per car. Registry, inspection and appraisal costs are not billed by us unless we agreed to pay them for you; then they are on an invoice of their own.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">An invoice we cancel shows Void with the reason, and the invoice that replaces it. Nothing is debited for a void invoice. Every invoice has Download PDF.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-the-monthly-debit-step-by-step" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The monthly debit, step by step</h2><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Notice day</span><em>10 days before: your invoices and one email with the total</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>The 15th</span><em>Each invoice is debited from your account</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Cleared</span><em>The invoice shows Paid and you get a receipt</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Insufficient funds?</span><em>A $50.00 Late Fee once, and the same amount tried again within 30 days</em></li></ol><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A debit is never more than its notice said. Each invoice shows &quot;will be debited on&quot; with the date.</li><li>If your bank returns a debit for insufficient funds, we add the $50.00 Late Fee to that invoice once and try the original amount again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of your Enrollment Agreement sets out. The Late Fee is collected with your next debit.</li><li>Returned for another reason (for example a closed account)? We do not try again and add no Late Fee. We pause your debit and email you: pay the invoice from its page, or set up a new account under Account &gt; Banking.</li><li>Returned again after the retry? The invoice is in arrears and we contact you.</li><li>Any debit that was missed and not paid since comes off your next monthly revenue statement: it shows there as a deduction with the invoice number.</li><li>You can always pay an invoice by card from its page before the debit day.</li><li>On your bank statement the debit shows our company&#39;s legal name, operating as CarmaCars.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">What each amount is</h3><p class="gd-p">Every debit email lists each amount in one line: the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment or late fee), the month it covers and how it was worked out. A car that joined during the month says &quot;prorated: 20 of 30 days&quot;. A car on a flat monthly payment pays no monthly fee for those days. Each line opens its invoice.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">When we can&#39;t collect a debit</h3><p class="gd-p">We email you, and our staff see the same reason:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>&quot;No bank debit set up&quot;: set it up under <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>. Nothing is taken until you do.</li><li>&quot;Owner cancelled the debit at their bank&quot;: set it up again under <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>.</li><li>&quot;Amount went up after the notice&quot;: we send a new notice for the new amount and debit it after the notice period.</li><li>&quot;The bank sent the payment back&quot;: see above. Pay the invoice from its page, or set up a new account under <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-set-up-the-automatic-debit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set up the automatic debit</h2><p class="gd-p">Do this once. Without it, we email you on each notice day to set it up.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>. Under Automatic debit of your fees, press <b class="gd-ui">Set up pre-authorized debit</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the agreement and press <b class="gd-ui">Continue to my bank details</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Enter your bank details and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the bank account</b>. Banking then shows the account and the next debit.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/banking</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/752"><img src="/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-52316739.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="752"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:96.2%;top:36.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-pay-an-invoice-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an invoice now</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Invoices, then the invoice. It lists what it covers and the balance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Card (paid at once) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay $...</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Or choose Pre-authorized debit (from a Canadian bank account, clears in 3 to 5 business days) and press <b class="gd-ui">Authorize debit of $...</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Prefer Interac e-Transfer? Send the amount to billing@carmacars.ca with the invoice number in the message.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/invoices/INV-1050</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/742"><img src="/guides/img/owner-06-invoice-desktop-bba2c020.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="742"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.9%;top:52.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.2%;top:52.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11.5%;top:80.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Paid us by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Once we record it, the invoice says &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on&quot; the date, you get a receipt by email, and the automatic debit does not take that amount. Paid part of it? The invoice shows Partly paid and only the rest is debited.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-tell-us-where-to-pay-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tell us where to pay you</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>. Under Where we pay you, choose Bank transfer or e-Transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in Account holder, Institution number, Transit number and Account number (or your e-Transfer email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit payout details</b>. For your security we confirm new details by phone before we use them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/banking</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:990/642"><img src="/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-87b2ffe3.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="990" height="642"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50.5%;top:25.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:90.9%;top:45.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:30.3%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-statements-and-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statements and payouts</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">This month so far, at the top of Statements: the rentals finished this month, your Owner Revenue, the Revenue Share, fees and deductions and the expected payout, worked out live and marked Provisional. Rentals still under way are listed below it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Statements: one a month, once approved by CarmaCars; the approved statement is the final one. Open one to see every booking, the revenue share, deductions and the payout.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download PDF</b> to keep a copy. We also email it to you with the PDF attached.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Payouts shows what was paid to you and when. Payouts are made on the 10th for the month before.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/statements/380cc1bb-bfd5-4e55-8022-93a3b998ca74</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/792"><img src="/guides/img/owner-09-statement-desktop-fc5f9ea5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="792"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16%;top:30.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:66%;top:40.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Paid a flat monthly payment for a car? Its statement shows a Flat monthly payment line for the month (a part month by the day) instead of the Revenue Share. The car&#39;s rentals are listed without amounts paid to you, as CarmaCars keeps them, and there is no insurance or tracker fee for it. A booking expense is taken off only when we charge it to you; it then shows as an owner cost with its reason. Vehicles shows the amount and since when.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from your statement</h3><p class="gd-p">If you agreed with CarmaCars to have your fees taken from your revenue statement, your invoices are not debited from your bank account. Each invoice is paid from your next owner statement (the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., 