  '<p class="gd-p">Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-invoices" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner invoices</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Invoices</b> tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner&#39;s and each application&#39;s Invoices tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> makes an invoice of any amount for an owner&#39;s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The monthly run and tracker invoices: <b class="gd-ui">Run the monthly invoices</b> issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); <b class="gd-ui">Issue all tracker invoices</b> bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/invoices</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1060"><img src="/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1060"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:22.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.7%;top:35.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-make-edit-and-issue-an-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Make, edit and issue an invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. <b class="gd-ui">Add a line</b> for more.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save as draft</b> to come back to it, or <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b> to send it now. On a draft&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Issue and email</b> sends it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid another way? Press <b class="gd-ui">Already paid outside the platform</b> on the invoice: choose how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or card outside the platform), the date and the reference. A draft is issued without the invoice email first, the payment is recorded, and the owner gets no email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the owner a receipt</b>. To record a smaller or extra payment, press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend email</b> sends the invoice again. <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b> opens it as a PDF.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-correct-an-issued-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct an issued invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b>, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press <b class="gd-ui">Void the invoice</b>. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Already paid? Void the payment first, or press <b class="gd-ui">Credit note</b> for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-the-automatic-debit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The automatic debit</h2><p class="gd-p">The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for payments the bank sends back and owners with no bank debit set up.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Notice day</span><em>Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Debit day</span><em>The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Cleared</span><em>The invoice is paid</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Returned, insufficient funds</span><em>The $50.00 Late Fee is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Returned for another reason</span><em>No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Scheduled and processing lists each debit. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b> holds one (a reason is needed).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners lists each owner&#39;s bank debit. Use <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send a notice now</b> or, with no bank debit set up, <b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/920"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="920"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.8%;top:21.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.5%;top:35.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91.5%;top:75.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:94.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:14.4%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.4%;top:89.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Insufficient funds: the $50.00 Late Fee is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner&#39;s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task. Any debit missed (returned for another reason, too late to retry, or a retry still waiting) comes off the owner&#39;s next revenue statement by itself: when the statement is built, the invoice goes in arrears (a waiting retry is cancelled) and the statement deducts it. Nothing to do.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner&#39;s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no bank debit set up gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-before-the-debit-day-the-debit-preview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Before the debit day: the Debit preview</h2><p class="gd-p">The top of the Debits tab shows the coming debit day.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Debit preview</b> lists each owner with something to debit: the total, whether a bank debit is set up, whether the notice went, and each invoice in one line: the amount, the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment, late fee), the period and how it was worked out, such as &quot;prorated: 20 of 30 days&quot;. The line opens the invoice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Something looks wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Hold</b> beside the owner and give the reason. Nothing is debited for that owner until you press <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Fee check</b> compares the month&#39;s invoices with each car&#39;s signed terms: no monthly fee on a flat monthly payment, a Turo-Only car, a shareholder&#39;s car or a company car, nothing before the Enrollment Date, and the amount the terms give. It changes nothing: void and reissue an invoice that does not match. Each production deploy prints the same check.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-when-a-debit-can-t-go-ahead" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a debit can&#39;t go ahead</h2><p class="gd-p">You get one email: &quot;Can&#39;t collect $X from the owner: the reason&quot;. The reasons are the words of the owner guide: no bank debit set up, owner cancelled the debit at their bank, amount went up after the notice, the bank sent the payment back. The email lists each amount in one line and has one button that fixes it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b> opens the Debits tab on that owner. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b> again there: the owner gets the email to set up their bank debit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a new notice</b> opens the same place with <b class="gd-ui">Send a new notice</b> for the new amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the invoice</b> opens the invoice to record a payment made another way.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b> tab</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Build all for a month</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Build one</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open each draft. Check it, <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> after a correction, <b class="gd-ui">Preview PDF</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Issue to the owner</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Reissue</b> sends a corrected copy; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> exports it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/400"><img src="/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="400"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:79.9%;top:27.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg" alt="An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-staff-commissions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff commissions</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Commissions</b> tab. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Not earned yet</span><em>The rental is ahead, or not paid in full</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pending approval</span><em>Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>You approved it; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded the payment; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Reversed</span><em>Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">By person shows each staff member&#39;s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Prices to review</b> lists prices typed by hand; <b class="gd-ui">Sourcing claims</b> lists staff who say they sourced a website request; <b class="gd-ui">Payments made</b> lists each payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Owner requests</b> lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company&#39;s share or of the cars&#39; rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change and approve</b> (your terms, with a note) or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner&#39;s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner&#39;s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced an owner: the owner&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Sourced by</b>. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month&#39;s rentals</td></tr><tr><td>An owner a salesperson brought in</td><td>The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars&#39;, a partner&#39;s or a shareholder&#39;s cars</td></tr><tr><td>Customer service, finance, fleet, field staff</td><td>10% (also the field referral fee)</td></tr><tr><td>Base</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off</td></tr><tr><td>On the owner statement</td><td>An owner&#39;s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner&#39;s car: from CarmaCars&#39; commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month&#39;s Sales tier) goes on the owner&#39;s next statement as an adjustment line.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-field-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Field pay</b> tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Clocked in and out</span><em>Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pay run started</span><em>Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>The figures are frozen, the period&#39;s hours are locked, the statements are numbered</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tab <b class="gd-ui">Pay run</b> shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings &gt; Program, Field pay). <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">After the period ends, press <b class="gd-ui">Start the payroll</b>: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). <b class="gd-ui">Refresh the figures</b> takes in a change made since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The period&#39;s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (<b class="gd-ui">Send again</b> repeats it). The statement&#39;s number opens its PDF; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> gives the run for your accountant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> lists everyone&#39;s shifts of the period. <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hourly rates</b> shows each person&#39;s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with <b class="gd-ui">Set the rate</b> (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Field pay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Overtime</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate</td></tr><tr><td>Vacation pay</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement</td></tr><tr><td>Deductions</td><td>None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer&#39;s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions that net to nothing</td><td>A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-model" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company model</h2><p class="gd-p">Money &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company model</b> is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b>: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months&#39; EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Actuals</b>: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental&#39;s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. <b class="gd-ui">Refresh actuals now</b> recomputes them at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pro forma 5 years</b>: each year&#39;s income statement, cash flow and key figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Assumptions</b>: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the assumptions</b>; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked &quot;From the actuals&quot; left blank uses the latest complete month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download as Excel</b>: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month&#39;s costs in Money &gt; Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-payroll-for-everyone-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payroll for everyone (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payroll</b> is one run every two weeks for the field staff (hours) and for customer service, Fleet and Finance (salary).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A salaried person is paid their monthly salary x 12 / 26, for the days they were employed in the period. The salary is their own (<b class="gd-ui">Set the salary</b>, with a reason), else the monthly pay they were hired at, else their role&#39;s (Program settings, va_salary_defaults), in US dollars unless set otherwise.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Finance prepares it: <b class="gd-ui">Start the payroll</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add a bonus or deduction</b> with the reason, then <b class="gd-ui">Send for approval</b>. You get an alert.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Record all payments</b> (one method and reference; each stub number is added to it) or <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> line by line. Each person gets their stub by email and in their portal.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Admin &gt; Team also has <b class="gd-ui">Schedules</b> (each role&#39;s days and hours, anyone&#39;s own, who is late today) and <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> (every staff member&#39;s KPIs for a week against the targets in Program settings).</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The townhall page: pick the craziest story, enter the week&#39;s social media figures, add the recording link, and mark anyone present or absent. Staff who miss two townhalls in a row are locked until you press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b> on the staff list.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each renter and lead shows an Intent card (hot, warm or cold, with the budget, car, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage they mentioned). The live map shows it on each pin. An AI reading fills the gaps within the free daily allowance only (Program settings, intent_ai_enabled).</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Investors see Search traction under the deck: Google clicks and impressions of the last 28 days, indexed pages and the weekly trend. Type the indexed pages from Search Console on the investor deck page under Investors (no API exists for it).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Monthly statements</b> tab: CarmaCars&#39; own monthly statement, in twelve sections.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Download <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b>, <b class="gd-ui">PDF by owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">PDF by vehicle</b>, or press <b class="gd-ui">Email me the PDFs</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Finalize</b> freezes the month. <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> works until then.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/reports</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:28%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.4%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.1%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.9%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from the revenue statement</h3><p class="gd-p">On an owner&#39;s page, the <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b> button sets <b class="gd-ui">How fees are paid</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit</b> (the default) or <b class="gd-ui">Take from revenue statement</b>. Taken from the statement, the owner&#39;s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;. Approved, the invoice reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task <b class="gd-ui">Invoice ... back to the bank debit</b>.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The flat-rate agreements</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b> instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner&#39;s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK</b> is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-how-it-s-paid-bank-debit-or-deducted-from-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How it&#39;s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit on the 15th</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> (taken from the owner&#39;s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On an invoice, <b class="gd-ui">How it&#39;s paid</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For the first and last month, choose <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> on the Terms tab (or at approval).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the Terms tab, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the agreed one-off fees</b> makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner&#39;s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-referral-links-between-owners-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Referral links between owners (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">When one owner referred another, open the referrer&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Referral links</b>, <b class="gd-ui">This owner referred another owner</b>: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner&#39;s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a <b class="gd-ui">Referral share</b> line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars&#39; share, never the referred owner&#39;s payout. With <b class="gd-ui">sees the cars</b> on, the referrer finds <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner&#39;s details. <b class="gd-ui">End</b> stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-statement-periods-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statement periods (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Statements run from the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th covers them. A rental that crosses the cutoff, or a long weekly or biweekly rental, is paid for the days inside each period, never twice. Each statement lists amounts still uncollected from the renter separately; they are paid on the statement after they are collected.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line', 'chapter', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'Every call and text on the CarmaCars number (Quo) is kept and matched to the person: staff, a renter and their booking, an owner or a lead. Staff answer texts from the same inbox as live chat. It is on by default; Program settings switch each part.

## The inbox

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**, the **Chat** tab, and press **Texts and calls**. Each number shows who it is (Renter, Owner, Lead, Staff or Unknown caller), unread texts and missed calls.
2. Choose a number. Calls and texts are in order; a call shows its length, and Quo''s summary or a one-line AI summary when there is one.
3. Write a text and press **Send text**: it goes from the CarmaCars number through Quo. **Suggest a reply** puts an AI draft in the box; nothing is ever sent until you press Send text.
4. Beside the conversation: the renter with their bookings, the owner or the lead. A caller who gave the same phone in live chat or a discount game shows their visit on the site.
5. **Stop texts** stops every text to the number, booking texts included. A person who texts STOP is stopped the same way; START allows texts again.

## Unknown callers

Press **Unknown callers**. For a number nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press **Create lead**, or find the renter and press **Link to** the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. **Match automatically again** undoes a link made by hand.

## Missed calls

A missed call raises the task "Missed call from ..." for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.

> Tip: Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, "Missed call: text the caller back"), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo''s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.

## Calls and texts on records

A renter''s page and a booking''s Messages & history section show the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries in the Activity log (chips **Texts** and **Calls**); an owner''s page has "Calls and texts". Calls are not recorded on the line for now, so there is no transcript or recording to show.

## The Activity log (release 35)

A renter''s page and a booking''s **Messages & history** section have one **Activity** log: everything about the renter, newest first, grouped by day. It holds the emails and account messages both ways and the emails the platform sent, the texts, the live chat, the calls with their summaries and next steps, the notes, the booking''s events, the payments and refunds, the documents, identity checks and signatures, and the visits to the site with what they did there and the signals.

1. **All** shows everything. Press a chip (Emails, Texts, Live chat, Calls, Notes, Booking, Payments, Documents and ID, Website) to see one type; press **All** to go back.
2. Type in **Search the activity** and press **Search** to find a word in the log; **Clear** takes it away.
3. 50 lines show at a time: **Older** shows the next 50, **Newest** goes back to the top.
4. **Email**, **Call** and **Text** are at the top of the log. An email from the renter has **Reply**, a text or call from them **Text** or **Call**, a chat line **Open the chat**.
5. **Add a note** is above the log; the note shows in it at once.

> Good to know: Payments show to Admins, customer service, Sales and Finance, as the booking''s Money section. The log never shows an email address or a phone number.

## Quo contacts

Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.

- A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site''s version is sent again.
- One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.
- A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.
- If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.
- **Settings**, **Quo contacts**: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and **Sync everyone again**. Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)", turn it off.

## Booking texts

Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and **Settings**, **Text alerts**).

## The settings

Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)": the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).


## Call and Text buttons

Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map''s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.

1. Press **Text**: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press **Send**. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person''s conversation under **Today** > **Visitors** > **Chat** > **Texts and calls**; press **Open the conversation** to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.
2. Press **Call**: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo''s desktop app is your computer''s calling app, tick **On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app** once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.
3. Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.
4. To use the phone''s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** in **Settings** > **Program**. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone''s own apps too.

## The CarmaCars app links

**Settings** > **Program**, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see **Download the CarmaCars app** in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.

## Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)

When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder''s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.

1. A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, **overdue** when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.
2. Write what the call was about in **Note about this call** and press **Add note**: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.
3. **Open the renter''s page** opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.
4. An unknown number shows **Unknown caller**: press **Create lead** to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.
5. Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).

## Renter notes (release 34)

Every renter page has **Add a note**, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip **Notes**): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press **Remove** and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter''s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal''s renter.

## The Call button through Twilio (release 35)
Quo keeps incoming calls, texts and AI answering. **Call** on a staff page rings the staff member''s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then **Call** opens Quo and says why.

Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, **Reveal** shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.

## Unanswered

**Leads** > **Unanswered** (customer service has it too): every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. **Reply** or **Call back** opens the conversation; **Mark answered** when it was answered another way. A customer waiting more than 15 minutes (Program settings, **Unanswered SLA minutes**) alerts customer service and the Admins once. WhatsApp is not in the list: the morning digest reminds you to check it.', 'Texts and calls (the Quo phone line)', 'Texts and calls in the chat inbox, unknown callers, missed calls, booking texts, call summaries and the settings.',
