- **Sales team** shows each person''s leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week or this month, best first.
- **Settings** > **Sales** sets how long a claim holds for renter, owner and partner leads (10 to 15 minutes suggested), the most a claim can be extended to, how many leads one person may hold, and how long a lead counts as hot.

> Good to know: Filters narrow the list by type, source, status, age, person and your own leads; the search finds a name, phone number, email or words they wrote.

## Rebooking, intent and leads (release 35)

- A returning renter''s new request goes straight to the salesperson of their last booking, with the usual claim time.
- Every renter and lead has an intent score (hot, warm or cold) with what they said they want: budget, car class, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage, read from calls (with their transcripts), texts, emails, the site chat and their visits.
- Leads are never given out by themselves: onboarded Sales claim them, one every 5 minutes, up to 3 open at once plus one for every 5 won in the last 30 days (at most 10).',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every lead in one place: people who are not renters or owners yet, from every source, with who is working on each one. Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All leads</b>. An alert for a new lead (in the app, on the phone, or by email) opens that lead&#39;s own page.</p><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-what-is-in-the-list" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What is in the list</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Renter leads</b>: the contact form, live chat, the phone number box, discount game claims, offers that expired, booking requests typed and not sent, calls missed from a number with no booking (they arrive by themselves within 15 minutes), and Live visitors who turned Hot and left an email.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>: owner program enquiries, owner applications started and not finished, owner form contacts and earnings calculator contacts. They are also under <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>, and each New owner program enquiry task opens its lead.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Partner leads</b>: fleet suppliers, dealers, rental businesses and insurers.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Each card shows the name, phone, email, the source in plain words (a live chat lead says Live chat), how old it is, and the start of what they wrote. New and hot leads come first. Open a lead for everything they wrote, the live chat transcript, their calls, every contact logged and the claim history.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-work-a-lead" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work a lead</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Claim</b> on a card, or <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> for the oldest hot lead nobody holds. It is yours for 15 minutes; nobody else can work on it meanwhile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>. Your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged on the lead. Each call, text, email or <b class="gd-ui">Note</b> adds another 15 minutes to your claim, up to 60 minutes from when you claimed it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Outcome</b> and choose Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won (with the booking number when there is one) or Lost (say why). Won and lost close the lead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing more to do? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark handled</b>. Done with it for now? Press <b class="gd-ui">Unclaim</b>: it goes back to the pool at once.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A claim that runs out returns the lead to the pool for everyone. One person holds at most 25 leads at a time. When a renter lead&#39;s person books and the booking is confirmed, the lead closes as Won by itself, for the Sales person on the booking.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-as-an-admin" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">As an Admin</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> gives a lead to a person (their claim, and the lead is assigned to them). <b class="gd-ui">Release</b> ends someone&#39;s claim.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Sales team</b> shows each person&#39;s leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week or this month, best first.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> sets how long a claim holds for renter, owner and partner leads (10 to 15 minutes suggested), the most a claim can be extended to, how many leads one person may hold, and how long a lead counts as hot.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Filters narrow the list by type, source, status, age, person and your own leads; the search finds a name, phone number, email or words they wrote.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="leads-and-sales-claims-rebooking-intent-and-leads-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rebooking, intent and leads (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A returning renter&#39;s new request goes straight to the salesperson of their last booking, with the usual claim time.</li><li>Every renter and lead has an intent score (hot, warm or cold) with what they said they want: budget, car class, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage, read from calls (with their transcripts), texts, emails, the site chat and their visits.</li><li>Leads are never given out by themselves: onboarded Sales claim them, one every 5 minutes, up to 3 open at once plus one for every 5 won in the last 30 days (at most 10).</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'academy', 'chapter', 'hiring', 'Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.

## Progress by staff member

1. Open **People** > **Academy**. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings > Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.
2. Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.
3. A section closed for them? Press **Open early**, give the reason and press **Open early** again. The reason is kept.

## Edit lessons and questions

1. Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.
2. **Edit the title** changes its name and what it covers.
3. Each lesson has **Preview** (the player) and **Edit the lesson**: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule.
4. **Add a lesson**, **Delete** a lesson; each question has **Edit** (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and **Delete**; **Add a question** at the end.

## The pass mark and the gate

- Settings > Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).
- Academy gate (on by default): a section opens only once the one before it is passed, and a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile (and Welcome). Every staff account is held until it passes: new hires from one-step Hire from the start, and the staff already working from release 34; their progress so far is kept. Admins are never held. Off: the academy only records progress.
- Release 33 added a section at the end of each path on what changed in releases 28 to 32 (bookings, handovers and returns; licences, photos and agreements; money; cars and listings), with its quiz.
- Take the Admin path yourself from **Take the Admin path**.

## The gate, Welcome and waivers (release 34)

- A new hire signs in to **Welcome**: four steps in order (welcome, their profile and phone, the academy, then their first-day tasks). While they are held, Welcome, the academy, the guide and their profile are all they open; any other page brings them back to Welcome.
- Each person''s progress is on their academy page (Admin > Academy, their name) and on their candidate page in Hiring, on the card **Academy gate**: held or open, and the sections passed.
- **Waive the academy** on that card opens their portal at once without the academy. Give the reason: it is kept in the audit log. **Take the waiver back** holds them again until they pass.
- Release 34 added four sections, each with its quiz: pickups and returns (check-in is the pickup, Sign and pay, Book it now, overrides), money (Charge the renter, holds, owner invoices paid outside the platform), listing photos from a shared folder, and the caller panel with renter notes. Staff who already passed see the new sections on their academy page; they are not held by them.
- Each section names the guide chapters it was written from. When one of those chapters is published again, the section is listed under **To review: the guide changed** on Admin > Academy: check its lessons and quiz against the guide, then press **Mark reviewed**.
', 'Academy', 'Training paths by function: progress, opening a section early, editing lessons and questions, the gate.',
